// with the uniq -c command above.
// #4031 then adds 1 run case (run_map_comma_ok_slot0), giving dRun=340.
// Derived with the uniq -c command above.
// #4066 (readonly) then adds 1 run case (run_readonly_field.bit), giving
// dRun=341. Neither branch bumped it: #4031 set 340 for its own fixture and
// #4066 added a case without touching this line, so both were right on their
// own base and the merge was wrong. Derived with the uniq -c command above.
// #3941 (conditional expression) then adds 1 run case
// (run_conditional_expr.bit) and #4182 (enum zero value) adds 1 run case
// (run_enum_omitted_zero_value) and 1 error case (error_enum_no_zero_value),
// giving dRun=343/dErr=139. BOTH branches wrote dRun=342 -- each was right
// on its own base and both were wrong here, and because they wrote the SAME
// wrong value the line merged with NO CONFLICT while only the comment above
