// Derived with the uniq -c command above.
//
// BOTH branched at 357 and BOTH correctly wrote 361 for their own four. Taking
// either branch's number leaves the count four short. This is the pinned-count
// merge collision the earliest entry above already names, and it is why every
// entry in this history says "derived" rather than "incremented": the only safe
// value is the one read off disk after the merge.
//
// dPanicDebug: #3087 (4 `overflow_trap_*_debug.bit` cases, `// panic-debug`;
// their 4 `overflow_trap_*_release.bit` siblings are ordinary `// run` cases,
// already counted in dRun) + #4220 (4 more `// panic-debug` cases,
// `dce_dead_overflow_*_debug.bit`, one per op), giving dPanicDebug=8. Unlike
// the #3087 four, the overflowing value here is never READ — `deadCodeElim`
// dropped the overflow-checked instruction, so the optimized `--debug` build
// silently did not trap.
//
// dRunDebug: #4052 adds 1 `// run-debug` case (run_debug_licm_zero_trip_no_trap.bit).
// #4333 (`for (i, x) in xs` pair binder) adds 1 run case
// (run_forin_pair.bit), giving dRun=358. It also REMOVES 1 error case,
// check_forin_pair_binder.bit: that fixture pinned `for (a, b) in m` as a
// PARSE failure (E0021, Appendix A's old `for_in = IDENT "in" expression`
// admitted no pair binder at all), which #4333 makes grammatical. The
// rejection moves to a real checker diagnostic instead (E0129, "the key is
// already inside the value") — a diagnostic this tree now introduces, so per
// this fixture's own header it belongs in _tests_/bit/checkercases/ under
// checkerdiag.bit's gate rather than here; check_forin_map_pair.bit there
// covers the identical case. Net dErr=143. Derived with the uniq -c command
// above.
// #4347 (for-of element fetched by the inline load, not `rt_call slice_get`)
// adds 1 `// run` case, run_forof_inline_elem.bit.
//
// #4352 adds 1 `// run` case (run_map_scalar_paths.bit), which drives the four
// map entry points' inline scalar-key probe through long chains, tombstone
// chains, reinsertion and a resize.
//
// #4347 and #4352 each wrote dRun=369 on their own branch and each was right
// there; merged together the tree holds 370. Re-derived off disk after the
// merge with the uniq -c command above, never carried over from a branch.
//
// #4358 (json key interning + jsonGet backward scan) adds 2 `// run` cases,
// giving dRun=372: json_get_last_wins.bit pins jsonGetFromObject's
// last-key-wins policy against the scan-direction change that would silently
// make it first-wins, and json_parse_key_intern.bit pins that the parser's
// key cache changes a key's identity and never its bytes.
//
// #4346 (string byte load emitted inline) adds 4 `// panic` cases,
// run_string_index_{neg,atlen,empty,nullfield}_panic.bit, giving dPanic=35.
// Its branch also read dRun=368, the value on the tree it was cut from, which
// two later merges had already moved. Three branches in one batch each wrote a
// correct count for a tree that no longer existed by merge time: the counts
// below come off disk, after the merge, and nowhere else.
// #4354 (the for-of element load's bounds test removed, the header having
// already made it) adds 1 `// run` case (run_forof_mutation.bit: append,
// reslice and rebind DURING the iteration, the null and empty bases, the
// packed and reference element arms) and 2 `// panic` cases
// (run_forof_index_{next,other}_panic.bit, which pin the ITERATION an ordinary
// `xs[j]` in a for-of body still panics at), giving dRun=371/dPanic=37 ON THIS
// BRANCH. Derived with the uniq -c command above, off disk, at commit time —
// and it is a claim about a tree that later merges will move: the three
// branches named in the paragraph above were each right on their own base and
// each wrong by merge time, so re-derive rather than trusting this line.
//
// #4358 adds 2 `// run` cases (json duplicate keys and the interning cache).
// Its branch read dRun=372/dPanic=35, correct on the tree it was cut from and
// wrong by merge time in BOTH fields: #4354 had already taken dRun to 371 and
// dPanic to 37. Merged, the tree holds dRun=373/dPanic=37. That is now FIVE
// branches in one batch each writing a correct count for a tree that no longer
// existed. The counts below are re-derived off disk after the merge and from
// nowhere else.
//
// #4353 adds 1 `// run` case (run_map_string_key_align.bit), taking dRun to
// 374. Per instruction it wrote NO census number at all and left test-golden
// red on its own branch, reporting the two census lines verbatim. That is the
// correct handling: a branch cannot know the tree it will merge into, and the
// five wrong counts above are what happens when it guesses.
//
// #4355 (the nil-function-value check) then adds 3 `// run` cases
// (run_nil_call_zero_trip.bit: a nil callee in a loop that runs zero times
// must NOT panic, the constraint any hoist of that check has to keep;
// run_closure_env_mutated_alloc_loop.bit: a MUTATED capture and an allocation
// in the same loop; run_closure_plain_captures_loop.bit: UNBOXED captures,
// the arm that catches a wrong env with a wrong VALUE and exit 0 rather than
// with a segfault) and 1 `// panic` case (run_nil_call_one_trip_panic.bit:
// one trip, same message as the straight-line case), giving
// dRun=374/dPanic=38 ON THAT BRANCH. Correct on its base and wrong by merge
// time -- the SEVENTH such count in this batch. Merged, the tree holds
// dRun=379/dPanic=38, re-derived off disk after the merge.

//
// #4371 (`append(dst, s)` appends a string's bytes in one call) adds 2 `// run`
// cases: run_append_str_bulk.bit (six lengths x four header states, each checked
// against the per-byte loop it replaces) and run_append_str_alias.bit (the E0214
// aliasing contract on the new path). Its branch read dRun=372/dPanic=35 —
// correct on its base, wrong by merge time in both fields, the SIXTH such count
// in this batch. Merged, the tree holds dRun=376/dPanic=37.
//
// #4356 adds 3 `// run` cases (a closure devirtualised through a CAPTURING
// lambda, one reaching an interface call, and an AMBIGUOUS site where two
// lambdas reach one instantiation and the `blr` must survive), taking dRun to
