//
// #4404 adds 1 `// run` case (run_exploded_pair_args.bit: a two-word aggregate
// parameter passed as two words, exercised through every use of such a
// parameter -- element reads, a traced word, reassignment, a loop-carried
// join, passing the aggregate on whole, forwarding it to another exploded
// parameter, a destructure, a call through a function value, a deferred call,
// and the nine-word argument-register boundary). IT WRITES NO CENSUS NUMBER:
// this branch leaves test-golden red reporting its two census lines verbatim
// (`run = 395, manifest says 394` and `scanned 661 cases, manifest totals
// 660`), so the counts below are re-derived off disk after the merge and from
// nowhere else. The `.expected` beside that case was generated by the
// PRE-#4404 compiler, which boxes the aggregate, so it is an oracle for the
// change and not a restatement of it.
//
// RE-DERIVED AT THE MERGE (`5a7c3ee7`): 661 files on disk, and counting each
// file's own directive line rather than its filename prefix gives run 395,
// error 143, panic 48, lint 43, fmt 10, panic-debug 8, types 5, ir 5, and one
// each of tokens, run-debug, doc, ast. Only `dRun` moved, 394 -> 395. Do not
// count by filename: `ls _tests_/cases/run_*.bit` returns 347 and `err_*`
// returns nothing at all, because the prefix is not the directive.
//
// #4405 adds 1 `// run` case (run_multiword_return.bit: a result handed back
// in more than one ABI return register -- two words, three words, a traced
// word beside an integer one, mixed int/float classes, the eight-word
// register budget and the nine-word shape past it, a sub-word member, a
// fallible result, a pass-through `return f()`, a whole tuple value returned,
// a `defer`, an element read off the call result, a call through a function
// value, and a discarded result). Every function in it carries a loop on
// purpose: an inlined callee's `ret` becomes a join-block edge and the return
// convention is never exercised at all. IT WRITES NO CENSUS NUMBER: this
// branch leaves test-golden red reporting its two census lines verbatim
// (`run = 396, manifest says 395` and `scanned 662 cases, manifest totals
// 661`), so the counts below are re-derived off disk after the merge and from
// nowhere else. The `.expected` beside that case was generated by the
// PRE-#4405 compiler, which boxes, so it is an oracle for the change and not
// a restatement of it.
//
// #4405 also REGENERATED `ir_tuple_layout.expected`, which is a different
// thing and is not an oracle: that golden pins the IR the change alters, so
// its expectation could only be taken after. `mixed(): (string, i64)` stopped
// boxing there, and it was one of only two `// ir` goldens repo-wide pinning
// `ptrs=[%N]` for a traced element -- so the case gained `tracedBoxed():
// (string, bool)`, whose sub-word member keeps it boxed, rather than letting
// that claim leave with the allocation.
//
// #4410 adds 1 `// run` case (run_exploded_pair_local.bit: a two-word aggregate
// LOCAL held as two words rather than as a box -- the loop-hoisted shape the
// change exists for, reassignment inside the loop, a traced word across the
// body's own allocations, use as one whole value, initialization from a call
// that returns the aggregate, a destructure, an arrow capture, a
// captured-AND-assigned name that must stay in a heap cell, an inner binding
// that shadows it, a nested aggregate, a call to a METHOD (which never
// explodes its parameters, so the handle has to come back), and a deferred
// call). IT WRITES NO CENSUS NUMBER: this branch leaves test-golden red
// reporting its two census lines verbatim (`run = 397, manifest says 396` and
// `scanned 663 cases, manifest totals 662`), so the counts below are
// re-derived off disk after the merge and from nowhere else. The `.expected`
// beside that case was generated by the PRE-#4410 compiler, which boxes the
// local, so it is an oracle for the change and not a restatement of it.
//
// #4410 also EXTENDED `run_exploded_pair_args.bit` with wide3/wide3Whole/wide4
// for #4412 -- a parameter of more than two words, which #4405 made reachable
// and which dropped every word past the second. Those three `.expected` lines
// are hand-computed arithmetic, not captured: the compiler that shipped #4405
// prints 120/450/1200 for them at exit 0, so it is not an oracle for that case.
// That is an edit to an existing file and moves no census count.
//
// #4406 adds 1 `// run` case (run_exploded_pair_keepalive.bit: an exploded
// aggregate whose word 0 is an INTERIOR raw pointer into the object word 1
// roots, read across a collection). `run` 398 -> 399, corpus 664 -> 665,
// re-derived off disk with `for f in _tests_/cases/*.bit; do head -1 "$f"; done`
// -- each file's own directive line, never its filename prefix. Its `.expected`
// is what the FIXED compiler prints; against merged `main` two of its four arms
// print 0, at exit 0, which is the whole reason the case exists.
//
// #4438 adds 1 `// run` case (run_string_compound_assign.bit: `s += "x"`
// through every lvalue shape -- local, class field, map entry, slice
// element). `run` 400 -> 401, corpus 666 -> 667, re-derived off disk the same
// way. Against merged `main` this fixture's output is nondeterministic
// (empty string or a panic reading a garbage pointer, across runs of the same
// binary) because compound-assign lowered string `+=` to a raw pointer `add`
// instead of the `string_concat` runtime call; its `.expected` is what the
// FIXED compiler prints, deterministically, which is the whole reason the
// case exists.
//
// #4076 adds 1 `// run` case (run_time_calarith.bit: std/time calendar
// arithmetic, clamping at month boundaries). `run` 401 -> 402, corpus
// 667 -> 668.
//
// #4439 adds 5 `// run` cases: a variadic class METHOD called at differing
// arities, and reached through a spread, an interface, `defer` and `init` --
// every method-call site skipped variadic-tail collection. `run` 402 -> 407,
// corpus 668 -> 673.
//
// THOSE TWO BRANCHES CONFLICTED HERE ON PURPOSE AND THAT IS THE GOOD CASE.
// #4076 was merged first and took `run` to 402; #4439 was cut when it was 401
// and wrote 406 for its own five fixtures. Both numbers were right on their
// own branch and both are wrong on merged `main`. Git conflicted because the
// two edits touch the same line -- had they not, the merge would have been
// clean and the count silently five short. Do not resolve this by arithmetic:
// re-derive off disk from each file's own DIRECTIVE line, which is what 407
// below comes from.
//
//   for f in _tests_/cases/*.bit; do sed -n '1,3p' "$f" \
//     | grep -oE '^// *[a-z-]+' | head -1; done | sed 's|// *||' \
//     | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn
//
// #4427 adds 1 `// run` case (the induction-copy coalescing guard). `run`
// 409 -> 410, corpus 677 -> 678. Re-derived off disk; this pair CONFLICTED
// because the two branches wrote different values, which is the loud form.
// The #4442 x #4443 pair wrote the SAME value and merged clean while being
// one short -- see the note above.

//
// #4461 adds 1 `// run` case (run_shortcircuit_shared_join.bit: `&&` under an
// enclosing `if` on the same condition, whose short-circuit join is the
// else-target of a `br` the arm64 backend folds -- the join has two
// predecessors and was being marked dead, so the then-arm ran
// unconditionally) and 1 `// panic` case
// (run_string_slice_shared_oob_panic.bit: two `s[lo:hi]` sharing one `oob`
// block, where only one of the two bounds `br`s folds and the surviving
// out-of-range edge fell through into the success path). Both FAIL on `main`
// at `3957fa28` -- 1 instead of 2, and exit 0 instead of a panic.
//
// RE-DERIVED OFF DISK, not incremented: 680 `.bit` files in `_tests_/cases`,
// each classified by its OWN line-1 directive in `directiveOf`'s exact prefix
// order (`// panic-debug` before `// panic`, `// run-debug` before `// run`),
// which is what `scanCorpus` reads -- `firstLine(src)`, golden.bit:361, line 1
// and no other. Do NOT widen that to the first few lines: several cases quote
// `// panic` inside the comment body below the directive. Result: run 411,
// error 145, panic 49, lint 43, fmt 10, panic-debug 8, types 5, ir 5, and one
// each of tokens, run-debug, doc, ast. Ten of the twelve are UNCHANGED, and
// that agreement is the control -- a derivation that disagreed with the ten
// counts nobody touched would be the instrument failing, not the tree moving.
// Only dRun (410 -> 411) and dPanic (48 -> 49) move, one apiece.
//
// #3838 (class field defaults) then adds 1 run case (run_field_default), 2
// error cases (error_field_default, error_trait_field_default) and 1 fmt case
// (fmt_field_default), #4467 adds 1 run case
// (run_ptrof_interior_keepalive.bit: a raw pointer from `ptrOf` recorded no
// keepalive edge, so its GC base was dead at the next safepoint and
// `*(ptrOf(s) + 1)` read after a collection returned 0 at exit 0), and #4469
// adds 1 run case (run_zeroval_boxed_enum_field.bit: a class's boxed-enum
// field left NULL by every construction form except the composite literal --
// `[]T(n)`, `let p: T`, an `init` object and a map miss all segfaulted on the
// first tag read), giving dRun=414 / dErr=147 / dFmt=11.
//
// THE SAME MERGE HAZARD FIRED TWICE IN A ROW HERE, one merge apart, and it is
// worth reading as a pattern rather than as two incidents. #3838 and #4467
// both wrote dRun=412; the value was short by one and only the COMMENT above
// it collided, which is the entire reason anyone looked. #4467 (landed at
// 413) and #4469 then both wrote dRun=413 against their own bases, and again
// only the comment collided. An identical bump is the COMMON case -- two
// branches each adding one case necessarily write the same number -- so the
// count line merges clean at a wrong value every time, and the prose that
// happens to sit above it is the only tripwire. Do not rely on it.
//
// RE-DERIVED OFF DISK after this merge with the `uniq -c` command above, not
// taken from either side: 686 `.bit` files in `_tests_/cases`, 414 `// run`,
// and the other ELEVEN counts byte-identical, which is the control -- a
// derivation that disagreed with a count nobody touched would be the
// instrument failing rather than the tree moving. Note the lint arm is three
// directives (`// lint exit=0` 21, `exit=1` 19, `exit=2` 3) summing to the
// single dLint=43, so a raw `uniq -c` shows fourteen lines against twelve
// counts.
//
// #3976 (`@json` on a class) adds 1 run case (run_json_attr) and 1 fmt case
